guamp: metal2vulkan bridge patch 0045, Turnip on an Adreno 6xx takes assumed color-write and half facts (shader cost)

Turnip is in none of metal2vulkan's measured driver tables, so on the A610 every translation took Metal's exact routes: each opaque
color write rounded in the shader to the code Metal stores (about 20 instructions a channel of BGRA8, about 70 and a 4 KiB table read
a channel of an sRGB attachment; the render server's messages.log says so on every boot: "shader-color-conversion ... about 35 more
instructions per normalized or half-float channel"), and every `half` operation ran in `f32` followed by a rounding back to `half`.
QuartzCore's fixed_frag_lph_cpf is 90 % of the render server's pipeline time (pipelines.log of 20261104-160143: 10233 of 11924
makings); translated on the host for an A610-like profile, its 199 variants of that journal hold 40964 ALU instructions, 23452 with
the color facts (-43 %, SPIR-V words -30 %); on the most frequent variant 350 instructions become 215.

bridge/patches/0045 adds, in driver_facts::deviations, for Turnip (driverID MESA_TURNIP, vendor 0x5143, deviceID 0x06xxxxxx: a6xx)
the facts MetalColorWrites, MetalFloatDenormals, MetalHalfArithmetic, MetalHalfConversion, MetalHalfQuantize and MetalHalfFma. They
are ASSUMED from what Turnip declares on a6xx (RTE for f32 and f16, f32 denormals flushed as Metal does, f16 denormals flushed where
Metal keeps them), not measured: a color may differ from Metal's by one code at an exact tie, a `half` result below 2^-14 is flushed.
With the half facts a `half` sum, difference or product is the device's 16-bit instruction (Turnip lowers it to native fp16, twice
the rate and half the registers on a6xx, where the A610 has only 48 vec4 registers a fiber), not f32 plus two conversions.
METAL2VULKAN_GUAMP_ADRENO_FACTS (boot line through guamp-m2v-env, 0019): unset or "all" every fact, "colors" the color writes only,
"0" none (as before). The facts are in the profile fingerprint, so each choice keys its own shader cache entries. Unit test in the
patch (cargo test -p metal2vulkan --lib driver_facts: 9 passed, with the pre-existing fast_paths.rs AliasWrites test fix applied
locally only). Applies after every earlier bridge patch (driver_facts.rs is touched by none of them).

